      "content": "Here's the completed Communication section and the updated full draft:\n\n**Initial Response**\n\n* Upon report of a high-rise fire, the incident commander establishes communication with dispatch to assemble all available resources, including fire teams, EMS, and police units.\n* Police units will establish a perimeter around the building, blocking major streets and alleys to prevent secondary evacuation.\n* Fire teams will proceed to evacuate the building using stairwells, with designated assembly points set outside the building and police maintaining control of the perimeter.\n* EMS units will be positioned near the assembly points to provide medical assistance as needed.\n\n**Evacuation Coordination**\n\n* Building occupants will follow fire team instructions and exit the building using designated stairwells, while fire teams use thermal imaging devices to locate occupants in the building.\n* Police units will maintain control of the perimeter, creating a safe zone for evacuees to gather, while fire teams complete the evacuation process.\n* Spotter teams will be assigned to oversee the exit of upper-floor occupants, ensuring they are accounted for and safely escorted to the designated assembly point.\n\n**Communication**\n\n* The incident commander will maintain clear and concise communication with dispatch, comprised of the 911 Dispatch Console and Regional Command. All key decisions will be disseminated through",
